                            <a name="comment2471"></a>
<h4 class="boldbyline">
Re: Return To Darkness
</h4>

<p>
I tried to post comments to this over the week-end and they didn't post. (I took it personally.)<br />
<br />
But, what I would have posted was that I remember reading these stories in the Times in the early '90s when I lived in Tampa. After I moved to Texas, I'd always look for the Bragg bylines on the big stories, Susan Smith, Oklahoma City. Then my brother gave me "All Over But the Shoutin'" and I read it through cover to cover in one sitting. The New York debacle was a bitter pill for we Bragg fans, and probably should not be forgotten, though it's also been dealt with here.<br />
<br />
But the point I'm making (and yes, I know I haven't been in a hurry to do it) is it's some 16 years or more later and I remember these Bragg stories. The man can write.
</p>
